      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The concept of meritocracy often functions as an ideological justification that naturalizes existing power structures, effectively obscuring the role of historical and institutional bias. Sociologically, this \"belief in pure merit\" allows dominant groups to dismiss systemic advantage as individual success, leading to an uncritical acceptance of the status quo. Therefore, advocating for wealth redistribution is a direct challenge to the myth of pure meritocracy, demanding we analyze *how* capital and privilege are unequally distributed before we judge individual \"worth.\"",
      "source": "target",
